findings.body:
`WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie` now sends `WebviewMessage::SetCookie`, so a delete request actually (re)sets the cookie.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1721"}

The event loop switches on the variant and invokes the matching wry method, so the `DeleteCookie` arm at ::file{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs"} line 3737 is now unreachable, and `webview.set_cookie(&cookie)` runs instead of `webview.delete_cookie(&cookie)`.

This silently changes the behavior of the public `Webview::delete_cookie` / `WebviewWindow::delete_cookie` APIs: an app that logs a user out by deleting the session cookie leaves the cookie in place (potentially refreshing its expiry). The PR description only asked to drop the redundant `cookie.clone()`, so this is not an intended behavior change.

::callout{type="warning"}
The original patch (`e384526`) correctly used `DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned())`; this looks like a copy/paste slip in the final head commit.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1718-1718"}
WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned()),

The `size`/`position` blocks were reordered and the whitespace was mangled:

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

`inner_size(size.width,    size.height)` has stray spaces and `position(position.x,position.y)` is missing a space after the comma. The repo's `.github/workflows/fmt.yml` runs `cargo fmt --all -- --check` on every PR (and AGENTS.md rule 3 makes passing rustfmt a hard requirement), so this will fail CI even though the code compiles.

The block order is semantically irrelevant (both calls just set `WindowBuilder` fields), so restoring the original order keeps the diff minimal:

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1316-1322"}
    if let Some(position) = features.position() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.position(position.x, position.y);
    }

    if let Some(size) = features.size() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.inner_size(size.width, size.height);
    }

`pub use tauri_runtime::Cookie;` (added at ::file{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/mod.rs"} line 23) is not just cosmetic. `webview_window.rs` imports `webview::Cookie` (line 39), and this PR removes the local `use cookie::Cookie;`, so without the re-export the module would not resolve `Cookie`. Both `tauri` and `tauri-runtime` pin `cookie = "0.18"`, so `tauri_runtime::Cookie` is the same type and there is no duplicate-type hazard.

It also reverts an accidental removal: the re-export existed in released 2.7.0 and was dropped by the unreleased #13661, so downstream users of `tauri::webview::Cookie` get their import path back. The `// Remove this re-export in v3` breadcrumb is sensible.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/mod.rs" lines="18-24"}
